@100  = ~Unbelievable! Just unbelievable!~
@101  = ~I know, right? Insane!~
@102  = ~Is something wrong?~
@103  = ~Oh, sorry, I didn't notice you there. It's nothing, really, I'm-—wait, you're an adventurer, aren't you? Maybe you could help. It's my friend, you see. He was taken by the Cowled Wizards!~
@104  = ~You saw this?~
@105  = ~Do you know where he was taken?~
@106  = ~I'm not interested in this.~
@107  = ~Well, no... But I know he must've been taken! He's a spellcaster, see, and he's disappeared! What else could've happened? But the damned beurocrats say that there's nothing that they can do, and they even deny that they took him at all!~
@108  = ~Go on.~
@109  = ~I wish. These damn beurocrats won't tell me! They say that they don't even know! Isn't that irresponsible, to let people lock other people up in some unknown location?~
@110  = ~But you're an adventurer. You work for money, don't you? I... I'm not naive enough to think you can free someone from the Cowled Wizards, but I'll pay you to prove that they're behind this!~
@111  = ~Alright. I'll try to find your friend. Do you have any leads?~
@112  = ~How much money are we talking?~
@113  = ~Thank you! He was last seen in Trademeet, but he's disappeared! I.. probably shouldn't tell you this, but if it helps... He likes to go to taverns. Perhaps a bit too much. I'd start there, if I were you. His name is Estelin.~
@114  = ~I can spare 2,000 gold. And this amulet of magic resistance! He gave it to me, just in case. Please, I just want to know what happened.~
@115  = ~Alright. I'll try to find Estelin. Do you have any leads?~
@116  = ~I... well, I can't force you. But I beg you to reconsider!~
@117  = ~Please go to Trademeet and find out what happened to Estelin!~
@118  = ~Have you found anything out?~
@119  = ~He... turned into a squirrel and wants to stay that way.~
@120  = ~ He WHAT!? And wants to WHAT!? He's... he's gone nuts! Oh, gods, he's gone insane. Lost it completely. I guess... well, if he's happier this way... But you'll want your reward, won't you? I promised you 2,000 gold and this amulet. I need to think about some things. Goodbye, and thank you for your help.~
